Chapter: ProbeClosureArity2Unsat

 The discriminator. Same `make2` as the saturated probe, but `half` names
 it with ONE of its two parameters -- a genuinely incomplete call, the
 same situation `add3` is in everywhere `add3` survives.

 `unsat 53` means SATURATION is the trigger: naming a definition
 incompletely is harmless, naming it completely corrupts it.
 A fault means merely being named by a partial application is enough,
 and saturation is not the discriminator after all.

Section: Shapes

  add4 : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add4 (w) (x) (y) (z) = w + x + y + z

  make2 : Integer, Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  make2 (a) (b) = (add4 a) b

 Names make2 with 1 of its 2 parameters. Defined, never called.

  half : Integer -> (Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer))
  half (n) = make2 n

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("unsat 53 expected: " & show ((((make2 5) 6) 20) 22))
  end
